hermes v0.23.0: nothing but the agent's systemd unit starts the agent's
gateway on a hyperhermes host.

Symptom (som, stefan, 2026-11-10 to 11-13): hermes-agent-stefan.service
exited 75 (TEMPFAIL) 1900+ times, "The host gateway already serves
profile 'default' - nothing to start ... PID 2937893". That PID was a
second `gateway run --quiet --idle-exit` in stefan's user manager, in the
transient scope of a cron job's external worker
(hermes-worker-cron-<job>-exec-<id>.scope), running for three days.

Cause: a deploy SIGTERMed the unit at 16:04:52 while a cron job
(`4-59/15 * * * *`) fired. Under a systemd-managed gateway, cron runs each
job in an external worker in a user scope (cron/scheduler.py,
_launch_external_cron_worker). The worker reaches the gateway through
run_canonical_job -> connect_gateway (hermes_cli/gateway_client.py) ->
ensure_gateway_runtime(idle_exit=True) (hermes_cli/gateway_runtime.py).
It found no owner, asked discover_existing_gateway_service, which only
knows units named hermes-gateway[-<profile>].service
(gateway_runtime_service._systemd), got None and spawned a detached
`gateway run --idle-exit` (gateway_runtime_start.spawn_unmanaged_gateway).
That gateway connected Telegram, so its idle exit (no adapters, no
clients) never fired. The unit's next start attached to it
(gateway/host_attach.decide -> ATTACH, transient) and exited 75 under a
supervisor, every 5 s, until someone killed the stray. The worker had the
right HERMES_HOME (the payload pins it); the `hermes_home` of
/var/lib/hermes/.hermes in gateway_state.json is a stale field that the
status writer never refreshes (gateway/status.py,
_prepare_runtime_status_update), the gateway.lock record was right.

Fix: hyperhermes exports HERMES_GATEWAY_MANAGED_UNIT=hermes-agent-<user>.service
and HERMES_GATEWAY_MANAGED_HOME=<the unit's HERMES_HOME> to every process of
the agent. For that home, and the named profiles under it that its gateway
multiplexes (hermes_cli/gateway_managed_unit.py):
  - ensure_gateway_runtime never starts a gateway: while the unit
    (re)starts, the client waits for it until its deadline (connect_gateway
    then fails with "starting: deadline", a cron run is marked failed and
    retried at its next slot) - the same wait a client already does for a
    unit that is starting. A unit that stays inactive or failed (nothing
    queued, for 10 s: a deploy's stop-then-start is not a stop) is reported
    at once, with the systemctl start / reset-failed hint;
  - spawn_unmanaged_gateway refuses (RuntimeStartError service_managed);
    `gateway restart --detach` prints the refusal and its hint instead;
  - run_gateway (every `gateway run`, `hermes gateway`; --force and
    --replace included) refuses first thing, before the respawn-storm log
    and its backoff, unless it is the unit's main process: SYSTEMD_EXEC_PID
    is its own PID and its cgroup is /system.slice/<unit> (a user unit of
    that name is not it). A child of the unit (a tool command, a cron
    worker) inherits SYSTEMD_EXEC_PID with a different value. start_gateway
    (also cli.py's gateway mode) keeps the same check as a backstop.
A standalone profile and every other home keep upstream's behaviour. To
bypass on purpose, unset the variables.

Checked by ../../../checks/managed-unit (offline, on the patched package).
Applied with fuzz 0 (../package.nix): a moved anchor fails the build.

